cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DELICTI, please cite it as below."
title: "DELICTI: corpus delicti for AI agents — mandate before act, independent witness to the deed, bonded consequence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziuba
    given-names: Alan
    affiliation: Dziuba Technology
repository-code: "https://github.com/dziuba0x/delicti"
url: "https://github.com/dziuba0x/delicti"
abstract: >-
  An accountability layer for autonomous AI agents on Flare. A principal commits a
  mandate on-chain before the agent acts; the effector's signed receipt is the first
  witness and a Flare Data Connector attestation of the effect on EVM chains or XRPL
  is the second; violations are computed over the whole sequence of deeds, so
  structuring is caught; and a bond is slashed in proportion to the breach, without a court.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-security
  - accountability
  - attestation
  - flare-network
  - flare-data-connector
  - xrpl
  - x402
  - model-context-protocol
  - slashing
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
